id: DRAFT-haveged-1.9.26-rndaddentropy-enotsup
trigger_tool: "runtime|configure|conan"
phase: "runtime|build"
error_signature: "RNDADDENTROPY ioctl on /dev/random returns ENOTSUP (errno 95) on HarmonyOS PC"
severity: 2
category: "ohos,entropy,ioctl,capability-boundary"
match_keywords: ["RNDADDENTROPY", "RNDGETENTCNT", "ENOTSUP", "haveged", "entropy daemon", "dev/random"]
root_cause: "The tested HarmonyOS PC device permits a read-only RNDGETENTCNT query but rejects even a zero-entropy RNDADDENTROPY request with ENOTSUP. A successful generator build is therefore not evidence that an entropy daemon can inject into the kernel pool."
affected_scope: "Programs that inject entropy into /dev/random via Linux RNDADDENTROPY; observed with haveged 1.9.26 on HarmonyOS PC aarch64. Other OHOS versions and privileges require their own probe."
rec_approach: "Probe RNDGETENTCNT and a zero-length/zero-entropy RNDADDENTROPY request before enabling an entropy-injection daemon. If ADD returns ENOTSUP, disable the daemon and expose only independently tested file/stream generation and library APIs. State that kernel injection is unverified/unsupported for this environment."
rec_command: "python3 rng-ioctl-probe.py  # O_RDWR|O_NONBLOCK /dev/random; GET before, ADD(0,0), GET after"
fallback: "If the product specifically requires kernel-pool injection, obtain a documented supported kernel interface or platform permission and re-probe; a file generator is not a substitute for kernel entropy injection."
safety_boundary: "Do not issue nonzero RNDADDENTROPY probes on production devices; a zero request establishes API behavior without crediting entropy. Do not infer all OHOS devices have the same result."
verify_builds: "haveged/1.9.26: Conan create and upstream make check 11/11; test_package 1/1"
verification_cmd: "python3 rng-ioctl-probe.py; conan create archives/h/haveged/1.9.26 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing"
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-haveged-1.9.26-rndaddentropy-enotsup.md
similar_to: "E556 (same 'probe capability, then narrow the deliverable' pattern; different errno family EPERM/EINVAL, different probe entry point, different narrowed scope); E400 (same 'runtime capability boundary' family; probes V8 flags and file permissions, not kernel device ioctls); E235 (compile/link-time getrandom entropy-source selection, not runtime ioctl availability)"
conflicts_with: ""
caused_by: ""
prescan_pattern: "RNDADDENTROPY.*ENOTSUP|RNDGETENTCNT.*RNDADDENTROPY|/dev/random.*ENOTSUP|errno 95.*random"
prescan_globs: "**/rng-ioctl-probe.py,**/*entropy*,*/*haveged*"
fallback_command: "python3 rng-ioctl-probe.py  # zero-entropy ADD probe; if ENOTSUP, keep the daemon disabled"
last_updated: "2026-10-17"
source_event: "haveged 1.9.26 HarmonyOS PC adaptation; GET=4038, ADD errno=95, GET=4038"
authors: "主理-6"
status: draft
draft: true
